DLM v0.0079 derives its model from the local DLM v0.0067/0068 Maru port,
following v0.0066's deductive design. Confirm DLM authorship/license before public
release; this NOTICE does not grant a license.

Maru sources and the evaluator binaries derive from attila-lendvai/maru
(https://github.com/attila-lendvai/maru), revision
3566784a063abbff264a249d6b061cf18afccd06. See LICENSE.maru.
The compiler-image build tools generate a modified evaluator with embedded
source payloads, memory reader, manifest, loader template and Maru generator.
Subsequent --self builds retain the compiler-image functionality. Working source
edits require rebuild mode; reproduce mode retains the embedded snapshot.

DLM0077 adds opt-in cooperative tasks to the existing Maru REPL reader,
Linux x86-64 poll readiness and native session file operations. DLM learning
semantics remain in src/dlm. No Shen implementation was copied or required.

DLM0078 adds a data-frame nondeterministic machine, checked proof-pattern
reuse, native reasoning-session replay and bounded propositional Beth/Craig
experiments. Screamer and OpenLogic are design references, not imported runtimes.
DLM0079 adds a Maru event space for shared G3c obligations, scoped
nondeterministic programs, subproof learning, proof-based propositional
interpolation and Beth definitions. Spatial coordinates are layout metadata.
No neural, Screamer, MLIR or other external runtime is imported.
DeepLog is a theoretical reference; no DeepLog implementation is included.
